n- `--skip-bad` unset on the same [good, bad, good] world: `TRAIN STOPPED ci: #2`, nothing merged — the default did not change.\n- CLI parse of `batch q.json` with no flags: `skip_bad=False, overlap=False`.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` → `merge_train self-test: 108 checks, 0 failed` (99 before this commit; the 9 new arms are listed above).\n- `bash tools/audit/seat/train.sh --self-test` → `train.sh self-test: ok (5 refusals shown)`; rc 0 (now six arms: the five refusals plus the child-argv shape).\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` → `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED` (seam_cut_total 762 <= 762, flat; `at_head` shares `one`'s tail rather than duplicating it).\n- `python3 tests/closure.py select --diff $(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)` → `MODE: SCOPED -- 2 script(s) run, 31 scoped out` (5 changed files; `tests/entities.py` and `tests/harness_headers.py` via `.github/workflows/governance.yml` from this branch's earlier commits — keyed on the mode line, not the count). Both are container-lane scripts with no local venv (Colima removed); their check-runs at this head are the citation.\n- `bash tools/pr/prepr.sh` → all ok, `PRE-PR: 4149e28ebd3f8cd668be107bc475cbc150280410`, exit 0.\n\n## Red checks\n\nnone — no check has gone red at this head. Any red the new CI runs produce will be answered here with the root-cause rule's cheaper detector or the finding that none exists.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone — both flags change only this instrument, whose own self-test and INSTRUMENTS.md entry pin them.\n\n## Friction\n\nnone.\n","created_at":"2026-10-12T04:38:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T21:37:22Z","closed_at":"2026-10-12T21:37:19Z","merged_at":"2026-10-12T21:37:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"d214c53a218f9169b0c6d4fde9351b4ec3121419","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2143/commits","review_comments_url":"htt